"Maximal Seshadri constants on arbitrary polarized surfaces (https://github.com/openai/math/tree/main/preprints/Maximal-Seshadri-Constants-on-Arbitrary-Polarized-Surfaces-September-23-2026)\nciteturn8academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Date: Wed Sep 23 00:00:00 2026 ... This resolves positively the qualitative Nagata–Biran conjecture for surfaces.\nTitle: Maximal Seshadri constants on arbitrary polarized surfaces\nAuthors: OpenAI\nDate: Wed Sep 23 00:00:00 2026\n\nWe prove that, for every smooth integral complex projective surface S and every ample line bundle L, the multipoint Seshadri constant at r very general points equals $\\sqrt{L^2/r}$ for every sufficiently large integer r. This resolves positively the qualitative Nagata–Biran conjecture for surfaces.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNagata Conjecture -- from Wolfram MathWorld (https://mathworld.wolfram.com/NagataConjecture.html)\nciteturn8search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Tevelev (2026) gives an expanded human exposition of a proof attributed to OpenAI. His stated theorem treats the equal-multiplicity case: a degree-Image: d plane curve with multiplicity at least Image: m>=1 at Image: r>=10 very general points satisfies Image: d>msqrt(r). ... Algebraic Blow-Up, Nagata-Biran-Szemberg Conjecture, Plane Curve, Seshadri Constant\n\n# Nagata Conjecture\n\nThe Nagata conjecture for plane curves predicts the strict degree-multiplicity inequality\n\nImage: dsqrt(r)>sum_(i=1)^rm_i \n\nfor a nonzero effective complex projective plane curve of degree Image: d>=1 at Image: r>=10 very general distinct points with prescribed nonnegative integer multiplicities Image: m_i no larger than the actual multiplicities. Repeated or reducible components and unequal multiplicities are allowed. Very general means outside a countable union of proper Zariski-closed subsets of the ordered configuration space.\n\nTevelev (2026) gives an expanded human exposition of a proof attributed to OpenAI. His stated theorem treats the equal-multiplicity case: a degree-Image: d plane curve with multiplicity at least Image: m>=1 at Image: r>=10 very general points satisfies Image: d>msqrt(r). The notes explain the argument rather than claim a new proof. The reported proof has not been independently verified here. This reference does not by itself verify every companion claim in the original announcement, including the higher-dimensional statements about Seshadri constants.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA Fourier approach to Gromov's filling area conjecture (https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08251)\nciteturn8academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Title: A Fourier approach to Gromov's filling area conjecture ... Date: Tue Sep  8 04:49:59 2026\nTitle: A Fourier approach to Gromov's filling area conjecture\nAuthors: Le Chen, Xiaolong Li, Yimin Zhong\nDate: Tue Sep  8 04:49:59 2026\n\nWe prove that every compact connected Riemannian isometric filling $M$ of a circle of length $2π$ satisfies $\\operatorname{Area}(M) \\geq \\frac{14ζ(3)}π \\approx 5.35677$, regardless of orientability or topological types. Our new approach uses the odd Fourier coefficients of the distance functions from boundary points. For orientable fillings, we use a cubic resonant perturbation to obtain $\\operatorname{Area}(M)>5.40154$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n039. Nagata’s conjecture and maximal Seshadri constants · math20 (https://math20.org/f/039/)\nciteturn8search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago;     `@misc{OAI:Nagatas-Conjecture-for-Plane-Curves-September-23-2026, ... This resolves positively the qualitative Nagata–Biran conjecture for surfaces.\n\n# Nagata’s conjecture and maximal Seshadri constants\n\n4 papers Lean\n\nProves Nagata's strict inequality \\(\\sum_i m_i\\lt d\\sqrt r\\) for every nonzero effective plane curve of degree d through r ≥ 10 very general complex points, with arbitrary multiplicities m_{i}. It also proves maximal multipoint Seshadri constants \\((L^n/r)^{1/n}\\) for every smooth polarized projective variety of dimension n ≥ 2 and all sufficiently large r: at very general points over ℂ, and at the geometric generic tuple over any algebraically closed field of positive characteristic.\n\n## Papers 4\n\n### Nagata's conjecture for plane curves\n\nOpenAI · September 23, 2026\n\nWe prove that a nonzero effective plane curve of degree d at r ≥ 10 very general complex points has total multiplicity strictly less than \\(d\\sqrt r\\). The inequality holds simultaneously for all curves, including reducible and nonreduced curves, and establishes Nagata's conjecture in its strict, nonhomogeneous form.\n\nRead PDF Download Source\n\nCite\n    \n    `@misc{OAI:Nagatas-Conjecture-for-Plane-Curves-September-23-2026,\n      author = {{OpenAI}},\n      title = {{Nagata's conjecture for plane curves}},\n      howpublished = {OpenAI Math Release preprint\n                      \\href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/Nagatas-Conjecture-for-Plane-Curves-September-23-2026/main.pdf}{OAI:Nagatas-Conjecture-for-Plane-Curves-September-23-2026}},\n      year = {2026}\n    }`\n\n### Maximal Seshadri constants on arbitrary polarized surfaces\n\nOpenAI · September 23, 2026\n\nWe prove that, for every smooth integral complex projective surface S and every ample line bundle L, the multipoint Seshadri constant at r very general points equals \\(\\sqrt{L^2/r}\\) for every sufficiently large integer r. This resolves positively the qualitative Nagata–Biran conjecture for surfaces.\n\nRead PDF Download Source\n\nCite\n    \n    `@misc{OAI:Maximal-Seshadri-Constants-on-Arbitrary-Polarized-Surfaces-September-23-2026,\n      author = {{OpenAI}},\n      title = {{Maximal Seshadri constants on arbitrary polarized surfaces}},\n      howpublished = {OpenAI Math Release preprint\n                      \\href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/Maximal-Seshadri-Constants-on-Arbitrary-Polarized-Surfaces-September-23-2026/main.pdf}{OAI:Maximal-Seshadri-Constants-on-Arbitrary-Polarized-Surfaces-September-23-2026}},\n      year = {2026}\n    }`\n\n### Maximal Multipoint Seshadri Constants in Higher Dimensions\n\nOpenAI · October 5, 2026\n\nLet L be an ample line bundle on a smooth integral complex projective variety X of dimension n ≥ 3. We prove that there is a threshold \\(r_0=r_0(X,L)\\) such that for every integer \\(r\\ge r_0\\), the ordinary multipoint Seshadri constant at r very general points equals the volume bound \\((L^n/r)^{1/n}\\). This establishes the qualitative Nagata–Biran–Szemberg assertion in these dimensions.\n\nRead PDF Download Source\n\nCite\n    \n    `@misc{OAI:Maximal-Multipoint-Seshadri-Constants-in-Higher-Dimensions-October-5-2026,\n      author = {{OpenAI}},\n      title = {{Maximal Multipoint Seshadri Constants in Higher Dimensions}},\n      howpublished = {OpenAI Math Release preprint\n                      \\href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/Maximal-Multipoint-Seshadri-Constants-in-Higher-Dimensions-October-5-2026/main.pdf}{OAI:Maximal-Multipoint-Seshadri-Constants-in-Higher-Dimensions-October-5-2026}},\n      year = {2026}\n    }`\n\n### Maximal multipoint Seshadri constants in positive characteristic\n\nOpenAI · October 5, 2026\n\nLet L be an ample line bundle on a smooth integral projective variety X over an algebraically closed field of positive characteristic, with \\(\\dim X=n\\ge3\\). We prove that there is a threshold \\(r_0=r_0(X,L)\\) such that for every integer \\(r\\ge r_0\\), the ordinary multipoint Seshadri constant at the geometric generic tuple of r points equals the volume bound \\((L^n/r)^{1/n}\\). The same conclusion holds in dimension two. This establishes the positive-characteristic form of the qualitative Nagata–Biran–Szemberg assertion at geometric generic tuples.\n\nRead PDF Download Source\n\nCite\n    \n    `@misc{OAI:Maximal-multipoint-Seshadri-constants-in-positive-characteristic-October-5-2026,\n      author = {{OpenAI}},\n      title = {{Maximal multipoint Seshadri constants in positive characteristic}},\n      howpublished = {OpenAI Math Release preprint\n                      \\href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/Maximal-multipoint-Seshadri-constants-in-positive-characteristic-October-5-2026/seshadri-positive-characteristic.pdf}{OAI:Maximal-multipoint-Seshadri-constants-in-positive-characteristic-October-5-2026}},\n      year = {2026}\n    }`\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNagata-Biran-Szemberg Conjecture -- from Wolfram MathWorld (https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Nagata-Biran-SzembergConjecture.html)\nciteturn8search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # Nagata-Biran-Szemberg Conjecture\n\n# Nagata-Biran-Szemberg Conjecture\n\nThe qualitative Nagata-Biran-Szemberg conjecture asserts that multipoint Seshadri constants of a fixed polarized variety attain their volume upper bound at sufficiently many very general points. For a smooth integral complex projective variety Image: X of dimension Image: n>=2 with ample line bundle Image: L, it asks for an integer Image: r_0(X,L) such that\n\nImage: epsilon(X,L;p)=(L^n/r)^(1/n) \n\nat very general distinct tuples for every integer Image: r>=r_0(X,L). The surface form is also called the qualitative Nagata-Biran conjecture. It asks for exact equality at each sufficiently large point count, rather than an asymptotic ratio.\n\nFor the projective plane the Nagata conjecture makes the sharper prediction starting at ten points, including a strict degree-multiplicity inequality.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfilling area conjecture source record | Conjecture Fieldbook (https://fieldbook.kineticgain.com/placements/open-filling-area-conjecture/)\nciteturn8search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawl